  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The diagonals \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\) of rectangle \\(ABCD\\) intersect at \\(O\\). Also, \\(AE\\perp BD\\) at \\(E\\), and \\(\\angle DAE=3\\angle BAE\\). Find the measure of \\(\\angle EAC\\) in degrees.",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "45",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\angle BAE=22.5^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle DAE=67.5^\\circ\\). In right triangle \\(ABE\\), \\(\\angle ABD=67.5^\\circ\\), so \\(\\angle ADB=22.5^\\circ\\). Since \\(OA=OD\\), \\(\\angle DAO=22.5^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\angle EAC=67.5^\\circ-22.5^\\circ=45^\\circ\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use congruent triangles\n\nThe perpendicular \\(AE\\) splits the right angle \\(DAB\\) into angles in the ratio \\(1:3\\), so \\(\\angle BAE=90^\\circ/4=22.5^\\circ\\). In right triangle \\(ABE\\), this gives \\(\\angle ABD=90^\\circ-22.5^\\circ=67.5^\\circ\\).\n\nTo find the angle made by \\(AC\\), compare \\(\\triangle BAD\\) and \\(\\triangle ABC\\). They have \\(BA=AB\\), \\(AD=BC\\), and \\(\\angle BAD=\\angle ABC=90^\\circ\\), so they are congruent by SAS. Corresponding angles give \\(\\angle BAC=\\angle ABD=67.5^\\circ\\). Both \\(AE\\) and \\(AC\\) lie inside the right angle at \\(A\\), so\n\\[\n\\angle EAC=\\angle BAC-\\angle BAE\n=67.5^\\circ-22.5^\\circ=45^\\circ.\n\\]",
